From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SenkOS
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 22:33:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] backlight: pwm_bl: honour default-brightness-level with the
 default table

Without brightness-levels, the backlight came up at half of the default
(CIE 1931) table, whatever the device tree said. Read
default-brightness-level for that table too, so a bootloader can set the
level the user left, and the panel lights at it.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/video/backlight/pwm_bl.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/video/backlight/pwm_bl.c b/drivers/video/backlight/pwm_bl.c
index 237d3d3f3..d15bd6254 100644
--- a/drivers/video/backlight/pwm_bl.c
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/pwm_bl.c
@@ -563,6 +563,10 @@ static int pwm_backlight_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			goto err_alloc;
 		}
 
+		/* Also in the default table's steps, e.g. set by the bootloader */
+		of_property_read_u32(pdev->dev.of_node, "default-brightness-level",
+				     &data->dft_brightness);
+
 		for (i = 0; i <= data->max_brightness; i++) {
 			if (data->levels[i] > pb->scale)
 				pb->scale = data->levels[i];
